1
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:02,544
WHAT, UH

2
00:00:02,586 --> 00:00:03,587
WHAT DID YOU...

3
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:04,713
WHAT?

4
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,758
I STILL LOVE YOU...

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,345
AND I KNOW I PROBABLY SHOULDN'T
EVEN BE HERE TELLING YOU THIS.

6
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:14,723
I MEAN, YOU'RE WITH CHANDLER,
A GUY I REALLY LIKE...

7
00:00:14,765 --> 00:00:15,724
AND IF YOU SAY HE'S STRAIGHT

8
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:16,767
I'LL BELIEVE YOU.

9
00:00:18,936 --> 00:00:19,979
AFTER SEEING YOU
THE OTHER NIGHT

10
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,563
I KNEW IF I DIDN'T TELL YOU

11
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:23,774
I'D REGRET IT
FOR THE REST OF MY LIFE.

12
00:00:23,816 --> 00:00:24,984
LETTING YOU GO WAS
THE STUPIDEST THING

13
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:27,611
I EVER DID.

14
00:00:27,653 --> 00:00:30,405
YOU KNOW, YOU'RE REALLY
NOT SUPPOSED TO BE BACK HERE.

15
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,324
UH, WELL, YOU KNOW, I'M SORRY.

16
00:00:32,366 --> 00:00:35,369
I KNOW THIS IS THE WRONG TIME
AND THE WRONG PLACE

17
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:36,787
BUT I HAD TO TELL YOU.

18
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:38,873
I WANT TO SPEND MY LIFE
WITH YOU.

19
00:00:38,914 --> 00:00:40,207
I WANT TO MARRY YOU.

20
00:00:41,876 --> 00:00:43,878
I WANT TO HAVE KIDS WITH YOU.

21
00:00:46,922 --> 00:00:48,215
OH, MY GOD.

22
00:00:48,256 --> 00:00:50,049
WHY DON'T THEY PUT CHAIRS
BACK HERE?

23
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:51,677
( yelps )

24
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:54,095
LOOK, I KNOW THIS IS CRAZY,
BUT... AM I TOO LATE?

25
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:55,096
WELL, Y...

26
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,431
YES, YOU'RE TOO LATE.

27
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:59,059
I MEAN, WHERE WAS
ALL THIS THREE YEARS AGO?

28
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,853
WELL, I KNOW,
I WAS AN IDIOT...

29
00:01:00,895 --> 00:01:02,396
AND I TRIED
TO FORGET YOU.

30
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:03,605
I-I REALLY DID.

31
00:01:03,647 --> 00:01:05,607
YOU KNOW, AFTER WE
HAD LUNCH LAST YEAR

32
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:07,234
I SPENT SIX
MONTHS IN AFRICA

33
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:09,236
TRYING TO GET YOU
OUT OF MY HEAD.

34
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:10,905
WHAT WERE YOU DOING
IN AFRICA?

35
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:12,406
WORKING WITH BLIND KIDS.

36
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:14,950
OH... WHAT ARE YOU DOING
TO ME?

37
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:18,412
OH, LOOK... I'M SORRY,
BUT, UM... IT'S...

38
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:20,748
THIS IS NOT GOING
TO HAPPEN.

39
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:22,123
OKAY, THAT'S FINE.

40
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:24,626
I'LL WALK AWAY, AND I'LL
NEVER BOTHER YOU AGAIN

41
00:01:24,668 --> 00:01:27,588
BUT ONLY... IF YOU TELL ME
THAT CHANDLER'S WILLING

42
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:29,214
TO GIVE YOU
EVERYTHING I AM.

43
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:30,591
WELL, HE IS.

44
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:32,509
YEAH, I MEAN...

45
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:34,970
MARRIAGE IS ALL
HE TALKS ABOUT.

46
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:36,722
OH, MY GOODNESS.

47
00:01:36,764 --> 00:01:39,224
IN FACT, I'M THE ONE
THAT'S MAKING HIM WAIT.

48
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:40,225
YOU ARE?

49
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:41,268
YEAH.
WHY?

50
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,270
WHY?

51
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:45,022
BECAUSE OF THE GOVERNMENT.

52
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:57,618
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

53
00:01:57,659 --> 00:01:59,912
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

54
00:01:59,954 --> 00:02:03,122
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

55
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:07,210
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

56
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:09,671
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

57
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:12,173
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

58
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:16,136
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

59
00:02:16,177 --> 00:02:22,101
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

60
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:28,649
ISN'T IT INCREDIBLE?

61
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:29,900
YEAH.

62
00:02:29,942 --> 00:02:32,444
MONICA AND CHANDLER
ARE GETTING MARRIED.

63
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:35,155
I KNOW. THEY'RE GOING
TO BE SO HAPPY TOGETHER.

64
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:36,364
OH... I MEAN

65
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:38,075
TWO BEST FRIENDS
FALLING IN LOVE--

66
00:02:38,117 --> 00:02:39,493
HOW OFTEN
DOES THAT HAPPEN?

67
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:40,368
NOT THAT OFTEN.

68
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,370
NO.

69
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,289
I'M SO HAPPY FOR THEM.

70
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:45,290
ME, TOO--

71
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:46,917
SO HAPPY FOR THEM.

72
00:02:46,959 --> 00:02:50,004
I'M SO HAPPY
AND NOT AT ALL JEALOUS.

73
00:02:50,045 --> 00:02:51,005
OH, NO.

74
00:02:51,046 --> 00:02:52,213
OH, GOD, DEFINITELY.

75
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:53,214
NOT JEALOUS.

76
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:54,215
MM-MMM.

77
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:55,216
( chuckles )

78
00:02:58,512 --> 00:03:00,472
I MEAN,
I'M PROBABLY 98% HAPPY

79
00:03:00,514 --> 00:03:01,807
MAYBE TWO PERCENT JEALOUS...

80
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:03,433
AND, I MEAN,
WHAT'S TWO PERCENT?

81
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:04,601
THAT'S NOTHING.

82
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:05,978
TOTALLY.

83
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:08,689
( sighs )

84
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:09,940
I'M LIKE 90%/10%.

85
00:03:09,982 --> 00:03:11,525
YEAH, ME, TOO.

86
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:16,195
HEY, UH...

87
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:18,490
HAVE YOU GUYS SEEN CHANDLER?

88
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,954
WELL, NO, BUT YOU KNOW
WHO DID STOP IN HERE

89
00:03:23,996 --> 00:03:24,997
LOOKING FOR YOU?

90
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:26,205
UM, TENNILLE.

91
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:35,674
SO, THAT MARRIAGE STUFF

92
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,675
THAT YOU WERE
SAYING YESTERDAY

93
00:03:36,717 --> 00:03:37,467
YOU DON'T REALLY

94
00:03:37,509 --> 00:03:38,468
BELIEVE THAT, DO YOU?

95
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:39,469
SURE, I DO.

96
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:40,804
IN FACT, I THINK

97
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:43,306
THE WHOLE CONCEPT
OF MARRIAGE IS UNNATURAL.

98
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:44,766
I MEAN, LOOK AT PIGS.

99
00:03:44,808 --> 00:03:47,644
LET'S TAKE A SECOND HERE
AND LOOK AT PIGS.

100
00:03:47,686 --> 00:03:50,271
OKAY, PIGS DON'T MATE
FOR LIFE.

101
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,815
I MEAN, A PIG CAN HAVE, LIKE

102
00:03:51,857 --> 00:03:53,984
A HUNDRED SEXUAL PARTNERS
IN A LIFETIME

103
00:03:54,026 --> 00:03:55,652
AND THAT'S
JUST AN ORDINARY PIG

104
00:03:55,694 --> 00:03:58,613
NOT EVEN A PIG
THAT'S GOOD AT SPORTS.

105
00:03:58,655 --> 00:03:59,948
WAIT A MINUTE.

106
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:01,992
ARE YOU HONESTLY
TELLING ME

107
00:04:02,034 --> 00:04:04,995
THAT-THAT YOU MAY NEVER
WANT TO GET MARRIED?

108
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:08,373
WELL, NEVER SAY NEVER,
BUT, YOU KNOW, PROBABLY, UM...

109
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:09,374
YEAH, NEVER.

110
00:04:09,416 --> 00:04:10,667
OH, MY GOD.

111
00:04:10,709 --> 00:04:13,336
TH-TH-THEN, WHAT
ARE WE EVEN DOING?

112
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:14,838
WHAT IS THIS?

113
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:18,092
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA,
WHAT IS ALL THIS PRESSURE?

114
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:20,677
IS THIS SOME NEW KIND
OF STRATEGY?

115
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:25,390
WHY DON'T YOU PUT DOWN YOUR COPY
OF THE RULES, HUH, MAN-TRAP?

116
00:04:25,432 --> 00:04:26,474
YOU KNOW WHAT?

117
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:27,601
I GOT TO GO.

118
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:29,686
( Monica sighs exasperatedly)

119
00:04:29,728 --> 00:04:31,021
IT'S OKAY.

120
00:04:31,063 --> 00:04:32,564
I GOT A PLAN.

121
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:39,947
WE'RE GOING
TO FIND LOVE.

122
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:41,198
DEFINITELY.

123
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:44,868
YEAH, I'M PRETTY CONFIDENT
ABOUT THAT.

124
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:46,745
THAT'S WHAT MAKES IT
SO EASY

125
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:49,831
FOR ME TO BE 80% HAPPY
FOR MONICA AND CHANDLER.

126
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:53,043
IT'D BE NICE TO HAVE
A LITTLE GUARANTEE, THOUGH.

127
00:04:53,085 --> 00:04:54,711
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

128
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:57,256
WELL, YOU KNOW, SOME PEOPLE
MAKE DEALS WITH A FRIEND

129
00:04:57,296 --> 00:04:59,216
LIKE, IF NEITHER OF THEM
ARE MARRIED

130
00:04:59,258 --> 00:05:01,802
BY THE TIME THEY'RE 40,
THEY MARRY EACH OTHER.

131
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:02,886
YOU MEAN A BACKUP?

132
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:03,845
YEAH, EXACTLY.

133
00:05:03,887 --> 00:05:05,639
YEAH, YEAH, I'VE GOT THAT.

134
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,306
YOU DO?

135
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:08,308
MM-HMM.

136
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:09,268
WHO?

137
00:05:09,308 --> 00:05:10,060
JOEY.

138
00:05:10,102 --> 00:05:11,061
JOEY?

139
00:05:11,103 --> 00:05:12,062
YEAH.

140
00:05:12,104 --> 00:05:13,396
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

141
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,232
YEAH, I LOCKED HIM IN
YEARS AGO.

142
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:20,612
WAIT, SO, IF NEITHER
OF YOU ARE MARRIED

143
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:22,114
BY THE TIME YOU'RE 40

144
00:05:22,156 --> 00:05:23,448
YOU'RE GOING
TO MARRY JOEY?

145
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:24,992
YEP, WE SHOOK ON IT.

146
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:26,743
YEAH... BUT BELIEVE ME

147
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:30,038
THAT IS NOT HOW HE
WANTED TO SEAL THE DEAL.

148
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,706
OH. SERIOUSLY?

149
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:32,749
OH, YEAH.

150
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:34,584
I THINK HIS EXACT WORDS WERE...

151
00:05:34,626 --> 00:05:36,503
( clicks tongue/kisses/growls)

152
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:38,880
CHARMING.

153
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:40,799
AH, HE'S JUST A BACKUP.

154
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:41,967
YEAH.

155
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:48,765
( chuckles )

156
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,350
HEY, MONICA.

157
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:53,728
HAVE YOU SEEN RACHEL...
OR A MIRROR?

158
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,522
THIS IS FOR MY BOAT.

159
00:05:55,563 --> 00:05:57,065
PRETTY COOL, HUH?

160
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:59,026
YEAH, IT'S GREAT.

161
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,027
WHOA, WHOA, WHAT'S THE MATTER?

162
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:02,070
TALK TO THE CAPTAIN.

163
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:04,739
I'M JUST HAVING
ONE OF THOSE DAYS

164
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:07,075
WHERE YOU REALIZE YOU'RE
IN A DEAD-END RELATIONSHIP.

165
00:06:07,117 --> 00:06:09,077
CHANDLER GIVING YOU
A HARD TIME, HUH?

166
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:10,996
IT'S NOT LIKE I WANT
TO GET MARRIED TOMORROW.

167
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:12,413
IT'S JUST I'D
LIKE TO BELIEVE

168
00:06:12,455 --> 00:06:14,415
THAT I'M IN A RELATIONSHIP
THAT'S GOING SOMEWHERE

169
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,917
THAT I'M NOT JUST
WASTING MY TIME.

170
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:17,127
WELL, YOU KNOW CHANDLER.

171
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:18,879
NO, I DON'T
KNOW CHANDLER...

172
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,047
NOT ANYMORE.

173
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,256
IT'S LIKE...

174
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:23,591
IT'S LIKE
SOMETHING'S CHANGED.

175
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:25,052
MAYBE YOU CHANGED.

176
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:27,386
I DIDN'T CHANGE.

177
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:29,514
MAYBE THAT'S THE PROBLEM.

178
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:31,892
WHAT?

179
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:34,311
CHANDLER IS A COMPLEX FELLOW

180
00:06:34,353 --> 00:06:37,314
ONE WHO IS UNLIKELY
TO TAKE A WIFE.

181
00:06:37,356 --> 00:06:39,149
WELL, WHAT DOES HE THINK?

182
00:06:39,191 --> 00:06:43,195
DOES HE THINK I'M JUST GOING
TO WAIT AROUND FOR NOTHING?

183
00:06:43,237 --> 00:06:46,781
MONICA, FACE IT, CHANDLER
IS AGAINST MARRIAGE

184
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,616
AN-AND ALWAYS WILL BE.

185
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,702
YEAH, WELL,
THERE'S SOME PEOPLE

186
00:06:50,744 --> 00:06:52,287
WHO DO WANT
TO MARRY ME.

187
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:53,288
THERE ARE?

188
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:55,290
YEAH-- RICHARD.

189
00:06:55,332 --> 00:06:57,625
RI-RI-RICHARD SAID
HE WANTS TO MARRY YOU?

190
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,169
MM-HMM.

191
00:06:59,211 --> 00:07:01,420
CHANDLER'S TELLING YOU
HOW MUCH HE HATES MARRIAGE?

192
00:07:01,462 --> 00:07:02,339
THAT'S RIGHT.

193
00:07:02,381 --> 00:07:05,217
CHANDLER LOVES MARRIAGE!

194
00:07:07,219 --> 00:07:09,428
YOU JUST TOLD ME THAT
HE HATES MARRIAGE

195
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:13,225
TH-THAT HE'S A...
A COMPLEX FELLOW WHO'S
UNLIKELY TO TAKE A WIFE

196
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:14,976
TH-THAT HE'S
AGAINST MARRIAGE

197
00:07:15,018 --> 00:07:16,144
AND ALWAYS WILL BE.

198
00:07:16,186 --> 00:07:18,813
YOU GOT THAT FROM WHAT I SAID?

199
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:26,487
RACH?

200
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,698
HEY, YOU.

201
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:29,824
HEY.

202
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:31,618
COME ON IN.
OH, THANK YOU.

203
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:35,080
HEY, YOU KNOW, I'M SO SORRY
TO HEAR ABOUT YOU AND ELIZABETH.

204
00:07:35,122 --> 00:07:36,164
OH, THANKS.

205
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:37,374
YEAH, I REALLY THOUGHT

206
00:07:37,416 --> 00:07:38,917
WE'D BE ABLE
TO MAKE IT WORK

207
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:41,460
BUT, UH... I GUESS IT
JUST WASN'T MEANT TO BE.

208
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:42,462
YEAH.

209
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:43,671
LOVE...

210
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:46,341
IT'S A TRICKY BUSINESS,
ISN'T IT?

211
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:48,843
I GUESS SO.

212
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:50,720
SO, WHAT DO YOU SAY
WE MAKE A PACT--

213
00:07:50,762 --> 00:07:53,390
IF YOU AND I ARE BOTH SINGLE
BY THE TIME WE'RE 40

214
00:07:53,432 --> 00:07:55,016
WE GET MARRIED.

215
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:57,477
I MEAN, WE KNOW EACH OTHER,
WE LIKE EACH OTHER...

216
00:07:57,518 --> 00:07:59,520
I MEAN,
WE'VE ALREADY SLEPT TOGETHER.

217
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:02,107
SO, YOU KNOW, THERE'LL BE
NO SURPRISES THERE.

218
00:08:02,149 --> 00:08:03,317
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

219
00:08:03,358 --> 00:08:04,692
NO, LIKE, WHAT'S THAT?

220
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:06,027
( laughing )

221
00:08:06,069 --> 00:08:07,695
SO, WHAT DO YOU THINK?

222
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:11,325
OH, YOU... YOU WANT
ME TO BE YOUR BACKUP?

223
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:12,326
EXACTLY.

224
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:14,577
OH, YEAH... I ALREADY HAVE ONE.

225
00:08:15,829 --> 00:08:16,913
WHAT? WHO?

226
00:08:16,955 --> 00:08:17,456
PHOEBE.

227
00:08:17,496 --> 00:08:18,457
PHOEBE?

228
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:19,458
WAIT A MINUTE.

229
00:08:19,498 --> 00:08:20,917
BUT SHE... BUT SHE JUST...

230
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,543
SHE SAID JOEY IS HER BACKUP.

231
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:25,422
( laughing ):
OH, I DON'T THINK SO.

232
00:08:25,464 --> 00:08:27,424
ROSS, I JUST HAD A CONVERSATION
WITH HER

233
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:29,676
AND SHE SAID
THAT SHE AND JOEY MADE A DEAL.

234
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:30,969
THAT'S IMPOSSIBLE.

235
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:33,013
I MEAN,
WE HAVE HAD A DEAL FOR YEARS.

236
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:34,764
WE-WE-WE SHOOK ON IT...

237
00:08:34,806 --> 00:08:38,143
ALTHOUGH, BELIEVE ME, SHE WANTED
TO DO A LOT MORE THAN THAT.

238
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:43,773
WHERE THE HELL HAVE YOU BEEN?!

239
00:08:43,815 --> 00:08:47,735
I WAS MAKING A COCONUT PHONE
WITH THE PROFESSOR.

240
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,029
( stammering )

241
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:52,657
RICHARD TOLD MONICA
HE WANTS TO MARRY HER.

242
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:53,867
WHAT?
YEAH, YEAH.

243
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:55,076
I'VE BEEN TRYING
TO FIND YOU

244
00:08:55,118 --> 00:08:56,577
TO TELL YOU STOP
MESSING WITH HER

245
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,038
AND MAYBE I WOULD HAVE

246
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,540
IF THESE DAMN BOAT SHOES
WOULDN'T KEEP FLYING OFF!

247
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:01,875
OH, MY GOD.

248
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:03,543
I KNOW, THEY SUCK!

249
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:06,046
HE'S NOT SUPPOSED TO ASK
MY GIRLFRIEND TO MARRY HIM.

250
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:07,422
I'M SUPPOSED TO DO THAT.

251
00:09:07,464 --> 00:09:08,173
I KNOW!

252
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:09,174
WELL, WHAT...

253
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:10,884
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M GOING TO DO?

254
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:13,512
I'M GOING TO GO OVER THERE,
I'M GOING TO KICK HIS ASS!

255
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:14,846
WILL YOU HELP ME?

256
00:09:16,348 --> 00:09:19,684
LOOK, CHANDLER, I
DON'T THINK US GETTING
OUR ASSES KICKED

257
00:09:19,726 --> 00:09:21,769
IS A SOLUTION, OKAY?

258
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:24,105
JUST GO AND FIND MONICA.

259
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:25,399
YOU'RE RIGHT. OKAY.
YEAH.

260
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,774
I'M GOING TO GET THE RING.

261
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,193
I'M GOING TO GET THE RING.

262
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:29,486
I'M GOING TO GO FIND HER

263
00:09:29,528 --> 00:09:31,154
AND I'M JUST
GOING TO PROPOSE.

264
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:32,280
OKAY.
OKAY, GO GET HER.

265
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:33,281
DUDE, DUDE, DUDE.

266
00:09:33,323 --> 00:09:34,199
HUH?

267
00:09:34,241 --> 00:09:34,991
LET ME KNOW

268
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:35,867
ABOUT THAT COCONUT PHONE.

269
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,827
IT MIGHT BE GOOD
FOR THE BOAT.

270
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:46,253
( knocking )

271
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:54,344
HI.

272
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:58,139
HI.

273
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:02,852
I DON'T WHY I'M HERE.

274
00:10:02,894 --> 00:10:05,105
I DIDN'T ASK.

275
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:08,525
YOU WANT TO COME IN?

276
00:10:08,567 --> 00:10:10,777
I DON'T KNOW.

277
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:11,945
OH, OKAY.

278
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:14,573
WELL, I'LL JUST LEAVE
THE DOOR OPEN

279
00:10:14,613 --> 00:10:16,991
AND GO SIT ON THE COUCH.

280
00:10:19,453 --> 00:10:21,496
CHANDLER IS SUCH AN IDIOT.

281
00:10:21,538 --> 00:10:23,039
DRINK?

282
00:10:23,081 --> 00:10:25,792
YEAH. I'LL HAVE
A SCOTCH ON THE...

283
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:26,751
ROCKS WITH A TWIST?

284
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:29,712
I REMEMBER.

285
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:33,592
YOU START SMOKING CIGARS?

286
00:10:33,632 --> 00:10:34,593
UH...

287
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:37,387
NO, NO. THAT'S ART.

288
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:41,475
IF IT BOTHERS YOU,
I CAN PUT MY ART OUT.

289
00:10:41,516 --> 00:10:46,104
NO, THAT'S OKAY.

290
00:10:46,146 --> 00:10:47,730
SO, MONICA...

291
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:50,942
LET ME ASK YOU
A QUESTION.

292
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,860
YOU KNOW, SINCE
WE BROKE UP

293
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:54,862
DO YOU EVER...
THINK ABOUT ME?

294
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:59,576
YEAH, ACTUALLY, I THOUGHT
ABOUT YOU A COUPLE MONTHS AGO.

295
00:10:59,618 --> 00:11:00,452
OH, REALLY?

296
00:11:00,494 --> 00:11:01,869
YEAH, BUT IT'S 'CAUSE

297
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:03,163
I HAD AN EYE EXAM

298
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,706
AND I DON'T LIKE
MY NEW EYE DOCTOR.

299
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,375
WHO IS IT?

300
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:08,460
EDWARD NEVSKY.

301
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:10,044
YEAH, HE'S NO GOOD.

302
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:17,718
DO YOU EVER THINK ABOUT ME
IN A... NON-EYE-DOCTOR WAY?

303
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,304
NO.

304
00:11:19,346 --> 00:11:22,890
AH.

305
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:24,643
BECAUSE GETTING OVER YOU

306
00:11:24,683 --> 00:11:27,812
IS THE HARDEST THING
THAT I'VE EVER HAD TO DO

307
00:11:27,854 --> 00:11:30,565
AND I NEVER LET MYSELF
THINK ABOUT YOU.

308
00:11:30,607 --> 00:11:34,361
( no audio )

309
00:11:37,989 --> 00:11:41,159
PHOEBE, YOU PICKED
JOEY AND ROSS?

310
00:11:41,201 --> 00:11:42,994
YOU CANNOT HAVE TWO BACKUPS!

311
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:44,412
OF COURSE I CAN.

312
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:47,624
IT'S JUST GOOD SENSE
TO BACK UP YOUR BACKUP.

313
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:50,126
LOOK, I'VE ALREADY LOST
CHANDLER.

314
00:11:50,168 --> 00:11:51,044
WHAT?

315
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:53,213
HEY, PHOEBE

316
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:54,964
WE'RE BOTH YOUR BACKUP?

317
00:11:55,006 --> 00:11:57,676
PHOEBE, HOW COULD YOU
DO THIS TO ME?

318
00:11:57,716 --> 00:12:00,387
I DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU'RE
COMPLAINING ABOUT NOW.

319
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:02,514
YOU WERE BOTH AWARE
OF THE SITUATION.

320
00:12:02,556 --> 00:12:04,683
NO, WE WEREN'T.
I WAS NOT!

321
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:07,352
OKAY, THIS KIND OF BACK TALK
IS NOT GOING TO FLY

322
00:12:07,394 --> 00:12:08,603
WHEN WE'RE MARRIED.

323
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:10,564
PHOEBE, YOU CAN'T HAVE
BOTH OF THEM.

324
00:12:10,605 --> 00:12:11,856
YOU HAVE TO PICK ONE.

325
00:12:11,898 --> 00:12:12,857
PICK ME!

326
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:13,983
NO, PICK ME!

327
00:12:14,025 --> 00:12:17,070
I DON'T WANT
TO END UP AN OLD MAID.

328
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,072
ALL RIGHT. WELL, LET'S SEE.

329
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:23,493
ROSS IS A GOOD FATHER,
BUT JOEY HAS A BOAT.

330
00:12:23,535 --> 00:12:25,245
THIS IS HARD.

331
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:26,371
THIS IS CRAZY.

332
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:27,664
LOOK, I WANT TO
SWITCH TO RACHEL.

333
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:29,290
OOH, I WANT TO SWITCH
TO RACHEL, TOO.

334
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,000
NO, JUST WAIT!

335
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:32,001
YOU GUYS

336
00:12:32,043 --> 00:12:33,253
WAIT, GUYS.

337
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:35,463
DON'T MAKE ANY RASH DECISIONS,
OKAY?

338
00:12:35,505 --> 00:12:37,215
JUST REMEMBER MY PROMISE:

339
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:40,843
IF WE GET MARRIED,
THREE TIMES A WEEK.

340
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,637
OH, GOD, PHOEBE.

341
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:44,556
I'M TALKING
ABOUT MASSAGES.

342
00:12:44,598 --> 00:12:45,890
OH, ALL RIGHT.

343
00:12:45,932 --> 00:12:47,559
( no audio )

344
00:12:50,604 --> 00:12:51,896
ALL RIGHT,
YOU KNOW WHAT?

345
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:53,273
I KNOW HOW
TO SETTLE THIS.

346
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,442
ALL RIGHT, THIS IS
WHAT WE'RE GOING TO DO.

347
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,569
I'M GOING TO WRITE
"JOEY" ON ONE NAPKIN

348
00:12:57,611 --> 00:13:00,655
AND I'M GOING TO WRITE
"ROSS" ON THE OTHER NAPKIN

349
00:13:00,697 --> 00:13:02,449
AND WE ARE GOING
TO PICK ONE

350
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:04,867
AND THAT PERSON IS
GOING TO BE OUR BACKUP, OKAY?

351
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:05,993
HERE WE GO.

352
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,786
THAT SOUNDS FAIR.
FINE.

353
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:08,787
GOOD.

354
00:13:08,829 --> 00:13:10,081
WOO-OO!

355
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,543
PICK ONE.

356
00:13:13,585 --> 00:13:15,545
LEFT.

357
00:13:15,587 --> 00:13:16,546
THANK YOU.

358
00:13:16,588 --> 00:13:17,756
YOU'RE WELCOME.

359
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:21,175
"ROSS."

360
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:22,427
"JOEY."

361
00:13:22,469 --> 00:13:23,886
HMM.

362
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:25,346
WE SHOULD JUST
SWITCH.

363
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:27,014
YEAH, ABSOLUTELY.

364
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:31,978
I MISS THIS APARTMENT.

365
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:34,981
NOW, THIS IS
A GROWN-UP'S APARTMENT.

366
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:36,274
I SHOULD BE WITH A GROWN-UP.

367
00:13:36,316 --> 00:13:38,025
DO YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

368
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:42,071
YEAH. YOU'RE SAYING YOU NEED
TO BE WITH SOMEONE MORE MATURE.

369
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:43,948
MAYBE SOMEONE WITH

370
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:48,077
A LICENSE
TO PRACTICE MEDICINE...

371
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:50,037
OR A MUSTACHE.

372
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:51,498
YOU KNOW, LET'S FACE IT.

373
00:13:51,539 --> 00:13:52,831
I'M NOT A KID ANYMORE.

374
00:13:52,873 --> 00:13:54,334
I NEED TO BE WITH SOMEONE

375
00:13:54,375 --> 00:13:56,461
WHO WANTS THE SAME THINGS
THAT I DO.

376
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:58,087
COMING TO MY PLACE OF WORK

377
00:13:58,129 --> 00:14:00,047
AND TELLING ME
THAT YOU LOVE ME--

378
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,549
I WANT THAT!

379
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:04,051
TALKING ABOUT PIG SEX
OVER LUNCH--

380
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:06,262
I DON'T WANT THAT!

381
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:09,098
I THINK THAT'S FAIR.

382
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:12,185
"FAIR"? PLEASE, DON'T EVEN TALK
TO ME ABOUT FAIR.

383
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:13,478
FAIR WOULD HAVE BEEN

384
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,647
YOU WANTING
TO MARRY ME BACK THEN.

385
00:14:15,689 --> 00:14:17,357
OR FAIR WOULD BE
CHANDLER WANTING

386
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:18,775
TO MARRY ME NOW.

387
00:14:18,817 --> 00:14:20,694
BELIEVE ME,
NOTHING ABOUT THIS IS FAIR.

388
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:22,195
NOTHING, NOTHING

389
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:24,364
NOTHING. NOTHING, NOTHING,
NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING!

390
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:28,618
IT'S OKAY. SHH, SHH.
HEY, HEY, SHH.

391
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:30,578
NOTHING.

392
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:36,584
I DON'T KNOW.

393
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:39,878
I DON'T KNOW. UM...

394
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,088
I KNOW.

395
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:45,218
I-I...

396
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:49,096
I HAVE TO FIGURE SOME,
YOU KNOW, SOME STUFF

397
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,557
BEFORE I CAN...

398
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:52,225
YEAH, I UNDERSTAND.

399
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:55,311
TAKE AS MUCH TIME
AS YOU WANT.

400
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:58,481
TEN, EVEN 20 MINUTES
IF YOU NEED IT.

401
00:15:00,066 --> 00:15:01,735
I'LL BE HERE...

402
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:02,943
NOT SMOKING.

403
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:10,951
( knocking )

404
00:15:18,209 --> 00:15:19,126
CHANDLER.

405
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,421
WHERE IS SHE?

406
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:23,381
I'M NOT SCARED OF YOU.

407
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:28,219
SHE'S NOT HERE
AND PLEASE COME IN.

408
00:15:28,261 --> 00:15:31,389
SCOTCH ON THE ROCKS,
WITH A TWIST...

409
00:15:31,431 --> 00:15:32,807
ON A COASTER--

410
00:15:32,849 --> 00:15:33,808
( chuckles )

411
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:35,101
MONICA? MONICA?

412
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:39,272
OKAY, SHE WAS HERE,
BUT SHE LEFT.

413
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:40,939
WHERE DID SHE GO?

414
00:15:40,981 --> 00:15:43,651
WELL, SHE SAID
SHE HAD TO THINK THINGS OVER.

415
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:44,903
OH, MY GOD.

416
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,279
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS,
YOU KNOW?

417
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,322
I THOUGHT...
I THOUGHT YOU WERE A GOOD GUY.

418
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:50,324
OH, HEY, LOOK, NOTHING HAPPENED.

419
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:51,868
NOTHING HAPPENED? NOTHING?

420
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:54,454
SO YOU DIDN'T TELL MY GIRLFRIEND
THAT YOU LOVE HER?

421
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:57,624
WELL, ALL RIGHT,
ONE THING HAPPENED.

422
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,250
YOU KNOW, I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

423
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:00,752
YOU KNOW WHAT YOU DID?

424
00:16:00,794 --> 00:16:02,837
MY GIRLFRIEND IS
OUT THERE THINKING THINGS OVER.

425
00:16:02,879 --> 00:16:04,380
YOU MADE MY GIRLFRIEND THINK!

426
00:16:04,422 --> 00:16:07,842
WELL, I'M SORRY.

427
00:16:07,884 --> 00:16:10,637
WHAT DOES SHE HAVE
TO THINK ABOUT?

428
00:16:10,678 --> 00:16:12,221
I LOVE HER.

429
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:14,140
WELL, APPARENTLY I'M WILLING
TO OFFER HER THINGS

430
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:15,767
THAT YOU ARE NOT.

431
00:16:15,809 --> 00:16:17,518
BUT I AM WILLING
TO OFFER HER ALL
THOSE THINGS.

432
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,978
THIS WAS JUST
A PLAN, YOU KNOW?

433
00:16:19,019 --> 00:16:20,396
A WAY TO THROW HER
OFF COURSE

434
00:16:20,438 --> 00:16:22,649
SO THAT WHEN I OFFERED
HER ALL THESE THINGS

435
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:23,858
SHE'D BE SURPRISED.

436
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:27,904
WELL, IF IT HELPS,
IT WORKED VERY WELL.

437
00:16:27,946 --> 00:16:30,156
WELL, IT WAS WORKING
UNTIL YOU SHOWED UP

438
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:34,243
YOU BIG TREE.

439
00:16:34,285 --> 00:16:36,329
I MEAN, THIS ISN'T FAIR.

440
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,956
YOU HAD YOUR CHANCE WITH HER.

441
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:39,874
YOU HAD YOUR CHANCE
AND YOU BLEW IT!

442
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:43,210
AND THIS IS MY CHANCE
AND I'M NOT GOING TO BLOW IT

443
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:45,630
BECAUSE WE ARE MEANT
FOR EACH OTHER.

444
00:16:45,672 --> 00:16:48,758
AND THIS HAS ALL JUST BEEN
ONE STUPID MISTAKE.

445
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:51,886
I WAS GOING TO PROPOSE TONIGHT.

446
00:16:54,305 --> 00:16:55,765
YOU WERE GOING TO PROPOSE?

447
00:16:55,807 --> 00:17:00,227
YEAH, I EVEN...
GOT A RING.

448
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:02,563
DID YOU GET A RING?

449
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:04,357
NO, I DON'T HAVE A RING.

450
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:11,238
YOU GO GET HER, CHANDLER.

451
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:17,411
AND CAN I GIVE YOU
A PIECE OF ADVICE?

452
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:19,956
IF YOU DO GET HER...

453
00:17:19,998 --> 00:17:22,166
DON'T LET HER GO.

454
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:23,751
TRUST ME.

455
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:28,006
YOU KNOW, RICHARD...

456
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:30,174
YOU ARE A GOOD GUY.

457
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,888
I KNOW.

458
00:17:34,929 --> 00:17:36,472
I HATE THAT.

459
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:50,820
DUDE...

460
00:17:50,862 --> 00:17:52,572
I CAN'T TALK TO YOU NOW.
I GOT TO FIND MONICA.

461
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:53,573
SHE'S GONE.

462
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:55,324
WHAT?

463
00:17:55,366 --> 00:17:57,410
SHE HAD A BAG
AND SHE LEFT.

464
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:58,578
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

465
00:17:58,619 --> 00:17:59,829
SHE WAS ALL CRYING.

466
00:17:59,871 --> 00:18:02,040
SHE SAID YOU GUYS
WANT DIFFERENT THINGS

467
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:03,708
AND THAT SHE NEEDED
TIME TO THINK.

468
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:05,752
WHY DIDN'T YOU TELL HER
IT WAS A PLAN?

469
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:07,712
I DID. I TOLD HER
EVERYTHING, CHANDLER

470
00:18:07,754 --> 00:18:09,255
BUT SHE WOULDN'T BELIEVE ME.

471
00:18:09,296 --> 00:18:10,548
WELL, WHERE...?

472
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:12,091
WHERE DID SHE GO?

473
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:13,342
TO HER PARENTS,
I THINK

474
00:18:13,384 --> 00:18:14,886
AND SHE SAID THAT
YOU SHOULDN'T CALL HER

475
00:18:14,928 --> 00:18:17,179
BUT IF I WERE YOU,
I WOULD.

476
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:19,766
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I RUINED THIS.

477
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:22,894
I AM SO SORRY, MAN.

478
00:18:22,936 --> 00:18:25,479
DAMN.

479
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:35,489
YOU WANTED IT
TO BE A SURPRISE.

480
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:47,460
OH, MY GOD.

481
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:58,805
CHANDLER, IN ALL MY LIFE

482
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:03,810
I NEVER THOUGHT
I WOULD BE SO LUCKY...

483
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:10,316
( voice breaking ):
AS TO FALL IN LOVE
WITH MY BEST...

484
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:12,568
MY BEST...

485
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:14,821
THERE'S A REASON WHY
GIRLS DON'T DO THIS!

486
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:15,989
OKAY, OKAY.

487
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:18,157
I'LL DO IT.

488
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:20,200
I THOUGHT...

489
00:19:24,622 --> 00:19:25,957
I CAN DO THIS.

490
00:19:27,374 --> 00:19:29,460
( chuckles )

491
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:34,173
I THOUGHT THAT IT MATTERED
WHAT I SAID

492
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,843
OR WHERE I SAID IT.

493
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:39,553
THEN I REALIZED

494
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:46,978
THE ONLY THING
THAT MATTERS IS THAT YOU...

495
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:48,855
YOU MAKE ME HAPPIER

496
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:51,024
THAN I EVER THOUGHT
I COULD BE.

497
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:56,029
AND IF YOU LET ME

498
00:19:56,070 --> 00:19:57,697
I WILL SPEND
THE REST OF MY LIFE

499
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,782
TRYING TO MAKE YOU FEEL
THE SAME WAY.

500
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,541
( chuckles )

501
00:20:09,375 --> 00:20:10,501
MONICA...

502
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:14,797
WILL YOU MARRY ME?

503
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:18,968
YES.

504
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:34,942
I KNEW YOU WERE LIKELY
TO TAKE A WIFE!

505
00:20:37,695 --> 00:20:39,155
Joey:
CAN WE COME IN YET?!

506
00:20:39,197 --> 00:20:40,406
WE'RE DYING OUT HERE!

507
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:43,159
COME IN! COME IN!

508
00:20:45,036 --> 00:20:45,953
WE'RE ENGAGED!

509
00:20:45,995 --> 00:20:48,873
( all cheering )

510
00:20:52,919 --> 00:20:57,548
OH, THIS IS THE
LEAST JEALOUS
I'VE EVER BEEN!

511
00:20:57,590 --> 00:20:59,466
OH, NO, WAIT! NO!
THIS IS WRONG!

512
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:00,467
ROSS ISN'T HERE!

513
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:01,928
OH.
OH.

514
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:04,055
OH, HELL, HE'S DONE
THIS THREE TIMES!

515
00:21:04,097 --> 00:21:05,514
HE KNOWS WHAT
IT'S ABOUT!

516
00:21:05,556 --> 00:21:06,515
YEAH!
YEAH!

517
00:21:06,557 --> 00:21:07,516
COME ON, BABY!

518
00:21:07,558 --> 00:21:08,559
HEY, HEY, HEY!

519
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:34,794
Captioned by
